SRC/ken -- ken, as built for OS-9/68000=======================================ken turns English into Cockney, with rhyming slang for much of thecomputer vocabulary: `computer' becomes `French Tutor', `file' `RoyalMile'.  Written by Stephen K Mulrine; from the `silly' collection ofjoke filters posted to alt.sources in December 1992.ORIG holds ken.l, its README and its Makefile as posted.ken.l is unchanged.  It is a lex program; lex.yy.c here was generated inuniverse with this disk's flex 2.3 from ken.l, as chef's, fudd's anddrawl's were.  ken.l carries its own main; yywrap.c supplies thetwo-line yywrap that lex's library `-ll' used to provide.  rand() islinked from /dd/LIB/rand.r; the random choices (`the bleedin'', `guv?',`mate!') are seeded from the process ID, as posted.    echo "What are you doing with my computer" | ken    Wotcher doin' wiv me French Tutor